Private Sector Survey on Cost Control in the Federal Govern­\nment. The Committee shall be composed of not more than 150 members  \nappointed by the President from among citizens in private life.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The President shall designate a Chairman from among the members of the  \nCommittee.\nS©c. 2. F u n ctio n s, (a) The Committee shall conduct a private sector survey on  \ncost control in the Federal Government and shall advise the President and the  \nSecretary of Commerce, and other Executive agency heads with respect to  \nimproving management and reducing costs.\n(b) The Committee shall conduct in-depth reviews of the operations of the  \nExecutive agencies as a basis for evaluating potential improvements in agency  \noperations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) In fulfilling its functions the Committee shall consider providing recommen­\ndations in the following areas:\n'(if Opportunities for increased efficiency and reduced costs in the Federal  \nGovernment that can be realized by Executive action or legislation;\n(2) Areas where managerial accountability can be enhanced and administra­\ntive control can be improved;\n(3) Opportunities for managerial improvements over both the short and lone  \nterm;\n(4) Specific areas where further study can be justified by potential savings;  \nand\n(5) Information and data relating to governmental expenditures, indebtedness,  \nand personnel management.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The heads of Executive agencies shall, to the extent  \npermitted by law, provide to the Secretary of Commerce, the Committee and  \nits staff units such information, including that relating to the structure, organi­\nzation, personnel and operations of the Executive agencies, as may be re­\nquired for carrying out the purposes of this Order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Members of the Committee shall serve without compensation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) A management office may provide overall administrative staff support to  \nthe Committee, guide the day-to-day operations of the Survey and provide  \nliaison with the Executive Office of the President; separate unit staffs may be  \nutilized to provide such staff support as is necessary to accomplish reviews of  \nindividual agencies.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) The Secretary of Commerce shall, to the extent permitted by law and  \nsubject to the availability of funds, provide the Committee with such informa-\n\n=== PDF page 14 of 328 ===\n28900 Federal Register / Vol. 47, No. 128 / Friday, July 2, 1982 /  Presidential Documents\ntion, administrative services, facilities, staff and other support services it may  \nrequire.\nJe) The Committee is to be funded, staffed and equipped, to the extent  \npracticable and permitted by law, by the private sector without cost to the  \nFederal Government. To accomplish this objective, it is expected that the  \nSecretary of Commerce will engage in a joint project, with a nonprofit  \norganization, pursuant to Section 1 of Public Law 91-412 (15 U.S.C. 1525), for  \nthe purpose of providing staff support to the Committee as described in  \nSection 3(c).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(d)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec3(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. G e n e ra l P ro visio n s,","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4 (lead-in)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Notwithstanding the provisions of any other  \nExecutive order, the responsibilities of the President under the Federal Advi­\nsory Committee Act, as amended, except that of reporting annually to the  \nCongress, which are applicable to the Committee established by this Order,  \nshall be performed by the Secretary of Commerce in accordance with guide­\nlines and procedures established by the Administrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) In accordance with the Federal Advisory Committee Act, as amended, the  \nCommittee shall terminate on December 31, 1982, unless sooner extended.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12369#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"47 FR 28899, PDF pages 13-14","sha256":"dda5465c092efabd8e4a5711bdf1b6b394794823d7edbc3908cb39a9e72939e4","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-07-02/pdf/FR-1982-07-02.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 10 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)","CONFLICT FULL_AND_PARTIA